            <ArticleTitle>Left testicular and groin pain: an unusual presentation for perforated appendicitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>771</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 12 yr old black male presented with a 3 day history of left inguinal and testicular pain associated with nausea, vomiting, and fever. Left groin exploration demonstrated a markedly inflammed patent process vaginalis containing purulent exudate. Concomitant abdominal exploration demonstrated a perforated gangrenous appendix with diffuse peritonitis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
